# artifacts a matrix case installs from the network, one line each:
#   SHA256  FILE  URL  LICENSE
# the digest is what a reviewer read at that URL, and the report prints it beside every
# case that used the artifact. a case whose artifact has no line here is an unpinned
# requirement with the URL named, never a silent pass, so nothing is downloaded during a
# report unless a case asks for it and no case depends on a digest nobody wrote down.
#
# wine-10.0.tar.xz also matches the sha512 entry in the signed sha512sums.asc that winehq
# publishes beside the tarball. a version that no longer exists is a failure here rather
# than a newer tag: a case names the version it was written for, not a series. zed moved
# its tags from 0.x to 1.x, so the pin names the release the case reads today.
#
